WEBVTT

00:18:28.075 --> 00:18:30.781
And they felt, you know, I think,

00:18:30.805 --> 00:18:34.624
a tremendous amount of agency
and ownership around --

00:18:35.390 --> 00:18:37.268
And then again, everyone felt this way

00:18:37.292 --> 00:18:40.580
to do the things you needed to do
to move the business forward.

00:18:40.604 --> 00:18:43.874
At least what we thought was moving
the business forward at the time.

00:18:43.898 --> 00:18:46.707
AG: That goes to a lot of the research
on strong cultures,

00:18:46.731 --> 00:18:49.239
which, there's a long list of benefits.

00:18:49.263 --> 00:18:52.024
We know that when organizations
have strong cultures

00:18:52.048 --> 00:18:54.739
they're better at attracting
and retaining people,

00:18:54.763 --> 00:18:56.635
because they stand for something unique

00:18:56.659 --> 00:18:58.707
and it draws talented employees,

00:18:58.731 --> 00:19:01.888
and once they're there,
why would I want to go anywhere else?